                analysisTableData: `
                    <tr><td>Scale of turnover</td><td>During the analysis period, the company employed 2,925 people, of which 492 left, resulting in an attrition rate of 17%.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Gender</td><td>Among women, the attrition rate was 15% (180 out of 1171), and among men 18% (312 out of 1754). The difference may stem from different career motivators.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Tenure in the company</td><td>The highest turnover affects people with a short tenure of 0-10 years (378 people, or 77%). Among employees with >20 years of experience, turnover is marginal (< 7%).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Job satisfaction</td><td>The number of resignations increases as satisfaction decreases. Interestingly, even among "very satisfied" employees (134 people) there are departures (e.g., for promotion elsewhere).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Monthly income</td><td>69% of those leaving (7 out of 10 people) earned less than $5,000. This indicator drops sharply after crossing the $10,000 threshold.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Age</td><td>Turnover is concentrated in the 26-35 age group (over 50% of all departures), which is the most mobile professional group. Above 45, departures decrease.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Education</td><td>Most departures are people with Bachelor and Master Degrees (65% of the total), indicating higher flexibility on the job market.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Department</td><td>R&D (282 departures, 57%) and Sales (186, 38%) generate the main staff fluctuation. HR notes high stability.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Highest turnover positions</td><td>Laboratory Technician (130), Sales Executive (113) and Research Scientist (99). These are highly specialized roles with performance pressure.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Professional experience</td><td>52% of those leaving had 0 or 1 previous job. Women more often leave with little experience, men - with extensive experience.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Distance from work</td><td>About 60% of those leaving live close to work, suggesting that commute is not the main reason for resignation.</td></tr>
                `,
                analysisListData: `
                    <li><strong>Departures are concentrated in the first years of work</strong><p>The most departures concern people in the early stages of employment (0-10 years), the company loses people just learning the organization. This means that onboarding is a key barrier.<br><strong>Recommendation:</strong> Introduce mentoring programs with regular feedback and a development map.</p></li>
                    <li><strong>High turnover in lower pay brackets</strong><p>Employees with earnings < $5000 account for nearly 2/3 of all departures, so they have an economic basis.<br><strong>Recommendation:</strong> Implement regular salary benchmarking in the sector.</p></li>
                    <li><strong>Satisfaction does not guarantee loyalty</strong><p>Over 25% of departures concern people satisfied with work. Comfort alone is not enough; development opportunities are crucial.<br><strong>Recommendation:</strong> Evaluation talks and transparent communication about promotions before employees look for alternatives.</p></li>
                    <li><strong>Different motivators by gender</strong><p>Men leave more often, especially in technical departments. Women prioritize comfort factors, men – development and salary.<br><strong>Recommendation:</strong> Improve employee-management communication, investigate managerial issues.</p></li>
                `,
                methodologyData: `
                    <ol class="methodology-steps">
                        <li>
                            <div class="methodology-step-header">
                                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M21.585 5.584L18.413 2.413a2.011 2.011 0 0 0-2.827 0L2.394 15.59a1.99 1.99 0 0 0-.583 1.21L1.24 21.75a1 1 0 0 0 1.01 1.01l4.95-1.173a1.99 1.99 0 0 0 1.21-.583l13.176-13.174a1.99 1.99 0 0 0 0-2.827zM17 4.53l2.47 2.47-2.58 2.58-2.47-2.47zM4.14 20.36l-1 .235.236-1L6.55 16.42l2.03 2.03zm4.24-3.12l-2.03-2.03L15.17 6.4l2.03 2.03z"></path><path d="M21 15h-5a1 1 0 0 0 0 2h5a1 1 0 0 0 0-2z"></path></svg>
                                <h3>Data Cleaning and Transformation in Power Query</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="methodology-content">
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Loaded data and analyzed it using <strong>Column Quality</strong>.</li>
                                    <li>Removed empty rows (<code>null</code>) that lowered data quality.</li>
                                    <li>Used first rows as table headers.</li>
                                    <li>Removed columns containing only <code>null</code> values.</li>
                                    <li>Achieved <strong>100% Column Quality</strong> for the entire dataset.</li>
                                    <li>Added a new <code>All Measures</code> table for centralized DAX measure management.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <div class="methodology-step-header">
                                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12 2.25c-5.385 0-9.75 4.365-9.75 9.75s4.365 9.75 9.75 9.75 9.75-4.365 9.75-9.75S17.385 2.25 12 2.25zM12.75 9a.75.75 0 0 0-1.5 0v2.25H9a.75.75 0 0 0 0 1.5h2.25V15a.75.75 0 0 0 1.5 0v-2.25H15a.75.75 0 0 0 0-1.5h-2.25V9z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path><path d="M7.22 7.22A.75.75 0 0 1 8.25 6h1.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5H9v.75a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0V7.22zM14.25 6a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v.75h-.75a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.75zM14.25 15.75a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75V18h-1.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.75v-.75a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75zM8.25 18a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75v-.75h.75a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5H8.25z"></path></svg>
                                <h3>Added Conditional Columns</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="methodology-content">
                                <ul>
                                    <li><code>Commuting Distance</code>: Classifies distance to work into: <em>Near by</em> (≤10 miles), <em>Far</em> (≤20 miles) and <em>Very far</em> (>20 miles).</li>
                                    <li><code>Working Years Group</code>: Groups tenure into ranges: <em>0-10</em>, <em>11-20</em>, <em>21-30</em> and <em>31+</em>.</li>
                                    <li><code>Job Satisfaction Status</code>: Converts rating into: <em>Very Satisfied</em>, <em>Satisfied</em>, <em>Dissatisfied</em>, <em>Very Dissatisfied</em>.</li>
                                    <li><code>Age bucket</code>: Corrects default age categorization with logical ranges.</li>
                                    <li><code>Companies Worked Bucket</code>: Groups the number of companies: <em>0-1</em>, <em>2-3</em>, <em>4 and more</em>.</li>
                                    <li><code>Monthly Income Balance</code>: Creates monthly income brackets.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <div class="methodology-step-header">
                                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 15a3 3 0 1 0 0-6 3 3 0 0 0 0 6z"></path><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.323 11.447C2.811 6.976 7.028 3.75 12.001 3.75c4.97 0 9.185 3.223 10.675 7.69.12.362.12.752 0 1.113-1.487 4.471-5.705 7.697-10.677 7.697-4.97 0-9.186-3.223-10.675-7.69a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.113zM17.25 12a5.25 5.25 0 1 1-10.5 0 5.25 5.25 0 0 1 10.5 0z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg>
                                <h3>Created DAX Measures</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="methodology-content">
                                <div class="dax-measure-block">
                                    <p><strong>Total Employees</strong>: Calculation of the total number of employees.</p>
                                    <pre><code><span class="dax-measure">Total Employees</span> <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-function">COUNTROWS</span>(<span class="dax-string">'Cleaned Data'</span>)</code></pre>
                                </div>
                                <div class="dax-measure-block">
                                    <p><strong>Total Attrition</strong>: Count of employees who left.</p>
                                    <pre><code><span class="dax-measure">Total Attrition</span> <span class="dax-operator">=</span> 
<span class="dax-function">CALCULATE</span>(
    [Total Employees], 
    <span class="dax-function">FILTER</span>(<span class="dax-string">'Cleaned Data'</span>, 'Cleaned Data'[Attrition] <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-string">"yes"</span>)
)</code></pre>
                                </div>
                                <div class="dax-measure-block">
                                    <p><strong>Attrition Level</strong>: Percentage attrition rate.</p>
                                    <pre><code><span class="dax-measure">Attrition Level</span> <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-function">DIVIDE</span>([Total Attrition], [Total Employees], <span class="dax-keyword">0</span>)</code></pre>
                                </div>
                                <div class="dax-measure-block">
                                    <p><strong>Attrition per department</strong>:</p>
                                    <pre><code><span class="dax-measure">HR Department</span> <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-function">CALCULATE</span>([Total Attrition], <span class="dax-string">'Cleaned Data'</span>[Department] <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-string">"Hr"</span>)
<span class="dax-measure">R&D Department</span> <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-function">CALCULATE</span>([Total Attrition], <span class="dax-string">'Cleaned Data'</span>[Department] <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-string">"R&D"</span>)
<span class="dax-measure">Sales Department</span> <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-function">CALCULATE</span>([Total Attrition], <span class="dax-string">'Cleaned Data'</span>[Department] <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-string">"Sales"</span>)</code></pre>
                                </div>
                                <div class="dax-measure-block">
                                    <p><strong>Gender percentage in attrition</strong>:</p>
                                    <pre><code><span class="dax-measure">Male Attrition</span> <span class="dax-operator">=</span> 
<span class="dax-keyword">VAR</span> total_attrition <span class="dax-operator">=</span> [Total Attrition]
<span class="dax-keyword">VAR</span> male_attrition <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-function">CALCULATE</span>([Total Attrition], <span class="dax-string">'Cleaned Data'</span>[Gender] <span class="dax-operator">=</span> <span class="dax-string">"Male"</span>)
<span class="dax-keyword">RETURN</span>
    <span class="dax-function">DIVIDE</span>(male_attrition, total_attrition, <span class="dax-keyword">0</span>)</code></pre>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <div class="methodology-step-header">
                                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 15a3 3 0 1 0 0-6 3 3 0 0 0 0 6z"></path><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.323 11.447C2.811 6.976 7.028 3.75 12.001 3.75c4.97 0 9.185 3.223 10.675 7.69.12.362.12.752 0 1.113-1.487 4.471-5.705 7.697-10.677 7.697-4.97 0-9.186-3.223-10.675-7.69a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.113zM17.25 12a5.25 5.25 0 1 1-10.5 0 5.25 5.25 0 0 1 10.5 0z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg>
                                <h3>Visualization and Template</h3>
                            </div>
                            <div class="methodology-content">
                                <p>The dashboard template was created in <strong>PowerPoint</strong> to ensure a consistent and professional look, and then imported as a background into Power BI.</p>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                `
            }
        };

        const setLocalLanguage = (lang) => {
            document.documentElement.lang = lang;
            document.querySelectorAll('[data-translate]').forEach(el => {
                const key = el.dataset.translate;
                if (translations[lang] && translations[lang][key]) { 
                    el.innerHTML = translations[lang][key]; 
                }
            });
            if(translations[lang]) {
                const map = {
                    'columnsTableBody': 'colsData',
                    'kpisTableBody': 'kpisData',
                    'analysisTableBody': 'analysisTableData',
                    'analysisListBody': 'analysisListData',
                    'methodologyTableBody': 'methodologyData'
                };
                for (const [id, key] of Object.entries(map)) {
                    const el = document.getElementById(id);
                    if(el) el.innerHTML = translations[lang][key];
                }
            }
        };

        document.querySelectorAll('.lang-btn').forEach(btn => {
            btn.addEventListener('click', () => setLocalLanguage(btn.dataset.lang));
        });

        window.showSection = function(id) {
            document.querySelectorAll(".info-section").forEach(s => s.classList.remove("active"));
            document.querySelectorAll(".toggle-btn").forEach(b => b.classList.remove("is-active"));
            document.getElementById(id).classList.add("active");
            document.querySelector(`button[onclick="showSection('${id}')"]`).classList.add("is-active");
        };

        document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
            const preferredLanguage = localStorage.getItem('preferredLanguage') || 'pl';
            setLocalLanguage(preferredLanguage);

            const mobileMenuToggle = document.getElementById("mobile-menu-toggle");
            if (mobileMenuToggle) {
                mobileMenuToggle.addEventListener("click", () => document.body.classList.toggle("nav-open"));
                document.querySelectorAll(".mobile-nav-menu a").forEach(t => t.addEventListener("click", () => document.body.classList.remove("nav-open")));
            }
            
            const lenis = new Lenis({
                duration: 1.5,
                easing: (t) => Math.min(1, 1.001 - Math.pow(2, -10 * t)),
                direction: 'vertical',
                smooth: true,
                smoothTouch: false,
                touchMultiplier: 2,
            });

            function raf(time) {
                lenis.raf(time);
                requestAnimationFrame(raf);
            }
            requestAnimationFrame(raf);

            const lightbox = document.getElementById("lightbox");
            const openLightbox = (src) => {
                lightbox.querySelector(".lightbox-image").src = src;
                lightbox.classList.add("open");
                lenis.stop();
            };
            const closeLightbox = () => {
                lightbox.classList.remove("open");
                lenis.start();
            };
            
            document.querySelectorAll(".project-image").forEach(img => {
                img.addEventListener("click", () => openLightbox(img.src));
            });
            lightbox.addEventListener("click", e => { if (e.target === lightbox) closeLightbox(); });
            lightbox.querySelector(".lightbox-close").addEventListener("click", closeLightbox);

            document.querySelectorAll(".kpi-card").forEach(t => {
                t.addEventListener("mousemove", e => {
                    const o = t.getBoundingClientRect();
                    t.style.setProperty("--mouse-x", `${e.clientX - o.left}px`);
                    t.style.setProperty("--mouse-y", `${e.clientY - o.top}px`);
                });
            });
        });
    </script>
</BaseLayout>